# Google Workspace CLI (gws) setup guide
## When to use
- Installing and initially configuring gws
- Separating personal and work accounts
- Debugging OAuth authentication errors
- Looking up Drive or Sheets API usage
## [WARN] Before installation: two tools share the same name
Homebrew provides **two conflicting tools** named `gws`.
| | `brew install gws` | `brew install googleworkspace-cli` |
|---|---|---|
| Purpose | Manage Git repository workspaces | Google Workspace API CLI |
| Desired tool | [X] | [O] |
Install `googleworkspace-cli`.
## Installation
```bash
brew install googleworkspace-cli
gws --version
# gws 0.16.0
```
There is no npm distribution; this is a Rust binary.
## Multiple Accounts
Separate configuration directories with
`GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_CLI_CONFIG_DIR`.
### Directory layout
```text
~/.config/
├── gws-personal/ # personal account
│ ├── client_secret.json
│ └── credentials.enc
└── gws-work/ # work account
├── client_secret.json
└── credentials.enc
```
### Create directories
```bash
# Copy the existing default configuration to personal
cp -r ~/.config/gws ~/.config/gws-personal
# Create the work-account directory
mkdir -p ~/.config/gws-work
```
### Define aliases in ~/.zshrc or aliases.zsh
```zsh
alias gws-personal='GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_CLI_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gws-personal gws'
alias gws-work='GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_CLI_CONFIG_DIR=~/.config/gws-work gws'
```
## Authentication with OAuth2
### Prepare a GCP project
1. Open [console.cloud.google.com](https://console.cloud.google.com).
2. Under APIs & Services → Library, enable required APIs such as Drive, Gmail,
and Sheets.
3. Under APIs & Services → Credentials, create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID.
4. Download `client_secret.json` to `~/.config/gws-{account}/`.
### Register test users while the app is unverified
> This is mandatory when the application has not completed Google verification.
1. Open APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen.
2. Under Test users, choose + ADD USERS and add the account email.
### Log in
```bash
gws-personal auth login
gws-work auth login
# Check authentication status
gws-personal auth status
# Success when "auth_method" is "oauth2"
```
## Usage examples
### Drive: search for files
```bash
# Basic search in My Drive only
gws-personal drive files list --params '{"q": "name contains '\''keyword'\''", "pageSize": 10}'
# Search all drives, including shared drives; these parameters are mandatory
gws-work drive files list --params '{
"q": "name='\''filename'\''",
"includeItemsFromAllDrives": true,
"supportsAllDrives": true,
"corpora": "allDrives",
"pageSize": 10
}'
# Shared spreadsheets only
gws-work drive files list --params '{
"q": "sharedWithMe=true and mimeType='\''application/vnd.google-apps.spreadsheet'\''",
"pageSize": 10
}'
```
### Sheets: read data
```bash
# Inspect spreadsheet structure and sheet names
gws-work sheets spreadsheets get --params '{"spreadsheetId": "SPREADSHEET_ID"}'
# Read data from one sheet
gws-work sheets spreadsheets values get --params '{
"spreadsheetId": "SPREADSHEET_ID",
"range": "sheet-name"
}'
```
## Gotchas
### Error 403: access_denied
**Symptom:** During login, the browser says `gws-cli has not completed the
Google verification process`.
**Cause:** The OAuth app is in test mode and the account is not registered as a
test user.
**Resolution:** GCP Console → OAuth consent screen → Test users → add the account
email.
### Shared-drive files do not appear in search
**Symptom:** `drive files list` returns no results.
**Cause:** Default search covers My Drive only and excludes shared-drive files.
**Resolution:** add these parameters:
```json
{
"includeItemsFromAllDrives": true,
"supportsAllDrives": true,
"corpora": "allDrives"
}
```
## Main environment variables
| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_CLI_CONFIG_DIR` | Configuration directory; the key to account separation |
| `GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_CLI_TOKEN` | Pre-issued OAuth2 access token |
| `GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_CLI_CLIENT_ID` | OAuth Client ID |
| `GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_CLI_CLIENT_SECRET` | OAuth Client Secret |
| `GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_PROJECT_ID` | GCP project ID |
## References
- [Official GitHub repository](https://github.com/googleworkspace/cli)
- [Drive API query syntax](https://developers.google.com/drive/api/guides/search-files)
The `gws-work` alias above is only an account-separation example. Actual runs
read `configDir` from `~/.jstack/profiles/<name>/workspace.json` and verify the
snapshot account immediately before a remote write.
